    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d427">

                <pb facs="0401" n="285" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg285"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 322.112J72/11.</note>
                <head ana="#head_untitled-inferred-from-preceding-sibling-head">[Untitled]</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 24.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Consulate General</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Guayaquil</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-03-13">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 13, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inform you that Mr.
                    Robert B. Jones, the American citizen who was illegally imprisoned, was
                    discharged March 11, 1914, at noon, under an opinion given by the judge a copy
                    of which is enclosed.<anchor n="8" xml:id="d427-f1"/>
                </p>
                <p>As stated by the judge, not a suspicion was ever against him, yet he, an innocent
                    man was compelled to pass three months in a filthy jail associated with the
                    vilest criminals, the neglect of his business having been the cause of his
                    financial ruin, as well as the loss of health of his wife.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Frederic W. Goding</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
